Vendored third-party dependency
===============================

  Library:  ultrahonk_soroban_verifier (Rust, no_std)
  Upstream: https://github.com/NethermindEth/rs-soroban-ultrahonk
            (originally yugocabrio/rs-soroban-ultrahonk)
  Commit:   c2160987260284c656ffbdad8344210fc162b177
            ("Merge pull request #42 from NethermindEth/chore/protocol27")
  Path:     crates/ultrahonk-soroban-verifier
  License:  MIT (see LICENSE)
  Audits:   internal review 2026-05-28; OpenZeppelin external audit
            2026-08-10 to 2026-08-28, findings resolved upstream before this
            commit (see VERIFIER_PROVENANCE.md)
  Target:   Barretenberg v0.87.0 UltraKeccakFlavor proofs (non-ZK, keccak
            transcript), i.e. `bb prove --scheme ultra_honk --oracle_hash
            keccak` from bb 0.87.0 / nargo 1.0.0-beta.9.

Source (src/), LICENSE, README.md, and VERIFIER_PROVENANCE.md are copied
verbatim from the commit above. Cargo.toml differs in two places only, both
because the crate is built here as a path dependency outside its own
workspace:

  - `soroban-sdk = { workspace = true }` became the version the upstream
    workspace pins at that commit, `{ version = "27.0.6", default-features =
    false }`;
  - the `[dev-dependencies]` table (upstream's test-utils crate and fixtures,
    which are not vendored) was dropped.

CHECKSUMS.sha256 pins every vendored file;
crates/perch-zk-adapter/tests/vendor.rs fails on any drift.

Updating
--------
Do not edit these files in place. Replace the directory wholesale from a new
upstream commit, re-apply the two Cargo.toml changes above, update this
NOTICE and CHECKSUMS.sha256, then regenerate the circuit artifacts
(`just zk-artifacts`) and re-run the adapter's real-proof tests. If the new
upstream targets a different Barretenberg version, the pinned toolchain in
scripts/zk-toolchain.sh and crates/perch-zk-prover must move with it: proofs
and verification keys from another bb version fail at the pairing check, not
at parse time.
